{"url": "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/departments/electrical-and-computer-engineering/graduate-programs", "final_url": "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/departments/electrical-and-computer-engineering/graduate-programs", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-14", "text": "Skip to main content\nEnter your keywords\nSearchsearch\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nDepartments\nResearch\nIndustry & Community\nLife at CECS\nAlumni & Friends\nAbout\nUM-Dearborn Home\nStudent One-Stop\nFaculty & Staff\nCommunity & Business\nAlumni\nApply\nGiving\nBrowse A-Z\nBreadcrumb\nHome College of Engineering and Computer Science Departments Electrical and Computer Engineering Graduate Programs\nIN THIS SECTION\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nOur Faculty & Research\nToggle Submenu\nLaboratories\nGraduate Programs\nThe Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering offers graduate programs across several engineering disciplines, taught by faculty who are experts in their fields, including two Fellows of the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE). Our graduates build successful careers in industry or continue their education through doctoral study.\nComputer Engineering, MSE\nElectrical Engineering, MSE\nEnergy Systems and Sustainability Engineering, MSE\nRobotics Engineering, MSE\nElectrical, Electronics, and Computer Engineering, Ph.D.\nElectrical and Computer Engineering, D.Eng.\nApply Now\nRequest Information\nMeet our Doctoral Students\nTake a look and learn more about our Ph.D. and D.Eng. students, their research interests, and the innovative work they are pursuing in electrical and computer engineering.\nECE Graduate Advising\nDoctoral Program Advising & Contact\nPh.D. students receive academic and research guidance from their assigned faculty advisor and mentor. For administrative questions about enrollment, program requirements, milestones, or graduation, contact the appropriate staff member below.\nAmanda Donovan\nDoctoral Program Coordinator\numd-ecegrad@umich.edu\n313-593-5420\nMengqi Wang\nDoctoral Program Director\nmengqiw@umich.edu\n313-593-5420\nMaster's Program Advising\nMeet Your Graduate Coordinator\nWelcome to the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering. As graduate coordinator, I can help answer questions, connect you with university resources, and support you throughout your academic journey.\nMichael Hicks\n313-593-5420 | umd-ecegrad@umich.edu\nOffice: 2050 IAVS\nMaster\u2019s Program Faculty Advisors\nComputer Engineering\nDr. H. Malik\nDr. S. Rawashdeh\nDr. A. Shaout\nProgram Director: Dr. Wencong Su\nElectrical Engineering\nDr. S. Awad\nDr. A. Hafeez\nDr. J. Hong\nProgram Director: Dr. Wencong Su\nEnergy Systems & Sustainability Engineering\nDr. C. Lee\nDr. G. Reyes-Villanueva\nProgram Director: Dr. T. Kim\nRobotics Engineering\nDr. J. Kwon\nDr. S. Rawashdeh\nProgram Director: Dr. A. Mohammadi\nCourse Catalog\nFind all the information you need in the course catalog\nPath to Degree\nLearn about the step by step journey you will take as a master's student\nTentative Future ECE Course Schedule\nCheck out when classes will be offered\nCECS Graduate Advising\nPlanning tools, policies, deadlines and more\nECE Directed Studies and Master's Thesis\nDirected Studies\nMaster's Thesis Guidelines\nRelated Resources\nCECS Graduate Advising\nRegistration\nOffice of Financial Aid\nCertificates\nDEARBORN\nFLINT\nANN ARBOR\n4901 Evergreen Rd\nDearborn, MI 48128, US\n313-593-5000\nContact us\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nX-Twitter\nYouTube\nMaps & Directions\nMy UM-Dearborn\nBookstore\nCanvas\nEmergency Information\nEmployment\nLibrary\nU-M Google Mail\nWolverine Access\n\u00a9 2026\nThe Regents of the University of Michigan Privacy Policy\n\" \"", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/departments/electrical-and-computer-engineering/graduate-programs#main"], ["", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs"], ["Undergraduate P